<title>UK: World 1996/97 cotton output revised marginally up.</title>
<headline>World 1996/97 cotton output revised marginally up.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, England 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cotton Outlook revised its 1996/97 world cotton output estimate upwards to 19.926 million tonnes in January from the 19.924 million estimated in December.</p>
<p>In 1995/96 the total was estimated at 19.92 million tonnes.</p>
<p>U.S. output was forecast at 4.126 against the December estimate of 4.064 estimate of million tonnes and 3.89 million in 1995/96. China's production was seen up 0.2 million tonnes at 4.0 million but down on 4.76 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Estimates were as follows, in thousand tonnes -</p>
<p>				 1995/96		   1996/97</p>
<p>			     Jan	 Dec	 Jan	   Dec</p>
<p>Northern belt</p>
<p> US			3,897    3,897	4,126	4,064</p>
<p> Egypt		     236	236	  336	  345</p>
<p> Turkey		    851	837	  750	  777</p>
<p> China		   4,767    4,767	4,000	3,800</p>
<p> India		   2,686    2,686	2,635	2,678</p>
<p> Pakistan		1,700    1,700	1,530	1,530</p>
<p> Uzbestan		1,250    1,250	1,060	1,060</p>
<p> Other cen. Asia	 556	556	  368	  393</p>
<p>Equatorial belt</p>
<p> African franc zone    687	687	  784	  845</p>
<p> Sudan		     106	106	   97	  143</p>
<p> Peru			 64	 72	   63	   63</p>
<p>Southern belt</p>
<p> Argentina		 425	425	  405	  425</p>
<p> S.Braz/cent	     296	296	  273	  273</p>
<p> North east		 24	 24	   27	   27</p>
<p> Paraguay		  110	110	   70	   75</p>
<p> Australia		 429	420	  568	  568</p>
<p> Others		  1,841    1,847	1,862	1,838</p>
<p> World		  19,924   19,914     18,954     18,903</p>
</text>
